 #:seon.task{:name "a-join-forks-main-after-both-needs-merge"
             :kind :function
             :intent "(hybrid-done-and-merge M10) Every assignment forks main once all its `:seon.task/needs` have a `:merged` assignment (decision C1; a Prove step's product merges into main like any change). Delete `:seon.task.attempt/fork`, `seon.task/attempt-rows-tx`, `seon.cluster.agent/seed-attempt!`, the predecessor clause of `seon.cluster.agent/fork-attempt!`, the `(first (sort fork-point))` pick and `plan-facts`' basis query; `seon.turn/fork-commit` reads `:seon.task/merge-base`; `seon.task` (629, 682) converted; the `:seon.task/assignment-row` map in `resources/seon/schemas/seon.task.edn` drops the fork member. Red proofs: `seon.cluster.db-flow-test/a-join-forks-main-after-both-needs-merge` (both needs' facts are in the successor's fork db) and `a-prove-steps-red-product-merges-into-main` (its red deftest and stub are on main after its merge; the Implement successor forks main and reads them red at its base). Cost: fork under 20 ms. Platform slice (`--test`); `src/seon/turn.clj` as a patch. After M8."
             :must-read #{seon.cluster.agent/fork-attempt! seon.cluster.agent/seed-attempt! seon.cluster.agent/plan-facts seon.task/attempt-rows-tx seon.task/ready seon.turn/fork-commit}
             :needs #{[:seon.task/sym seon.cluster.squash/a-merge-whose-reached-definition-moved-writes-nothing] [:seon.task/sym seon.task/a-done-branch-merges-with-no-merge-request-written-by-the-agent]}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/chain-experiment-2.md" "docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/hybrid-done-and-merge.md"}}]
